---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const title = "Commands & Settings | PaneCrew Docs";
const description =
  "Every panecrew.* command and setting the PaneCrew VS Code extension contributes, and how to bind your own keyboard shortcuts to them via VS Code's keybindings.json.";

// Kept in sync by hand with apps/extension/package.json's own
// contributes.commands / contributes.configuration — that package.json is
// the single source of truth VS Code itself reads; this table is a reader-
// friendly mirror of it, not a second registry.
const commands = [
  { id: "panecrew.openProjectGrid", title: "PaneCrew: Open Project Grid…" },
  { id: "panecrew.addFolderToGrid", title: "PaneCrew: Add Folder to Grid…" },
  { id: "panecrew.applyCompactLook", title: "PaneCrew: Apply Compact Look" },
  { id: "panecrew.restoreLook", title: "PaneCrew: Restore Default VS Code Look" },
  { id: "panecrew.savePreset", title: "PaneCrew: Save Current Grid as Preset…" },
  { id: "panecrew.loadPreset", title: "PaneCrew: Load Grid Preset…" },
  { id: "panecrew.deletePreset", title: "PaneCrew: Delete Grid Preset…" },
  { id: "panecrew.searchInFolder", title: "PaneCrew: Search in Folder…" },
  { id: "panecrew.insertSnippet", title: "PaneCrew: Insert Snippet…" },
  { id: "panecrew.refreshExplorer", title: "PaneCrew: Refresh Explorer" },
  { id: "panecrew.setPaneCrewTheme", title: "PaneCrew: Set PaneCrew Theme…" },
];

const settings = [
  { key: "panecrew.grid.defaultColumns", default: "2", description: "Default column count for a new project grid." },
  { key: "panecrew.grid.defaultRows", default: "2", description: "Default row count for a new project grid." },
  { key: "panecrew.grid.defaultProjectsFolder", default: "\"\"", description: "Folder the file picker opens in for \"Open Project Grid…\", \"Add Folder to Grid…\", and \"Open Project in New Window…\". Empty means VS Code's own default location." },
  { key: "panecrew.compactLook.hideStatusBar", default: "true", description: "Whether Compact Look hides the status bar." },
  { key: "panecrew.compactLook.hideMinimap", default: "true", description: "Whether Compact Look hides the editor minimap." },
  { key: "panecrew.git.showDecorations", default: "true", description: "Show git status badges/colors in the PaneCrew explorer." },
  { key: "panecrew.snippets.defaultScope", default: "workspace", description: "Where newly saved snippets are stored by default (workspace or global)." },
];
---
<DocsLayout title={title} description={description} path="/docs/cli/" active="cli">
  <article class="docs-md">
    <h1>Commands &amp; settings</h1>
    <p>
      PaneCrew doesn't have its own CLI flags or a hardcoded shortcut registry. As a VS Code
      extension, it contributes ordinary VS Code commands and settings, and keyboard shortcuts are
      bound the same way you'd bind any other command: through VS Code's own
      <code>keybindings.json</code>.

    </p>

    <h2>Commands</h2>
    <p>
      Every command below is available from the Command Palette (<code>⌘⇧P</code> /
      <code>Ctrl+Shift+P</code>) by typing its title. To bind a keyboard shortcut to one, open the
      Keyboard Shortcuts editor (<code>⌘K ⌘S</code> / <code>Ctrl+K Ctrl+S</code>), search for the
      command title, and assign a key — or add an entry directly to <code>keybindings.json</code>:
    </p>
    <pre><code>{`{
  "key": "ctrl+alt+g",
  "command": "panecrew.openProjectGrid"
}`}</code></pre>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Command</th><th>Command ID</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {commands.map((c) => (
          <tr>
            <td>{c.title}</td>
            <td><code>{c.id}</code></td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Settings</h2>
    <p>
      Configurable from the Settings editor (search "PaneCrew") or directly in
      <code>settings.json</code>:
    </p>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Setting</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {settings.map((s) => (
          <tr>
            <td><code>{s.key}</code></td>
            <td><code>{s.default}</code></td>
            <td>{s.description}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p>
      Compact Look never hides the activity bar, regardless of settings — that row stays visible
      in PaneCrew's standard look by design.
    </p>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
